# Phase 5 T-U2 (the Ctrl-O reading position across a page rebuild, fx
# 026a8f4e, b1a53b01). Five reads make a document taller than the screen;
# then a command whose heading wraps to two rows while it is `Running` and
# fits one as `Ran`. Ctrl-O while it runs, a page up so the view stops
# following, then the same view after the command settles: its heading loses
# a row, a `* network:` record lands above the view, and the answer lands
# below. The first rows of the two snaps say whether it held. fx's
# `shell`/`run` is xfx's `terminal`/`exec`; TZ=UTC on both (T-U5).
fx: gateway p5-transcript-anchor-turns.json
xfx: gateway p5-transcript-anchor-xfx.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
env TZ=UTC
work p5-transcript-ws
wait 4
type read and wait
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap running
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-running
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup2
wait 10
snap full-pgup2-after
key C-o
wait 1
snap end
gwlog
